+\section{Additional separator audit, 21 October 2026}
+
+A new clean execution of the standalone separator, using its unchanged
+pinned scientific sources, ended with
+\code{FRESH_GLOBAL_SEPARATOR_PASS} in 180.92 seconds. The 109 local
+charts, 436 coordinate faces and all other boundary pieces passed, with
+zero unresolved cells. All 330 directly comparable scientific files
+were byte-identical to the archived outputs; boundary and separation
+records agreed after explicitly removing path, timing and derived-hash
+fields. All 454 fresh-output hashes were checked. This is an additional
+separator execution; the complete three-package optimality execution
+reported above remains the original one.
+
+An independent implementation using Python integers and exact rational
+arithmetic verified all 715 geometric inclusions: eight Gram and inverse
+entries, 218 center coordinates, 109 squared transverse norms and 380
+neighbor distances, as well as three scalar maxima. It computes inner
+products through the full-lattice degree-four Laplacian of zero
+extensions and checks boundary zeros. It does not import the supplied
+C++ interval engine. These checks validate the fixed geometry; they do
+not constitute an independent interval evaluation of the critical-state
+residuals or chart energies. Code, negative controls and complete records
+are included in \code{verification_notes/separator_2026_10_21}.
+
+The separator's historical minimum checker prints bare decimal scalars.
+Its downstream consumer already adds or subtracts an exact $10^{-18}$
+padding to every numerical baseline field it uses. For the fixed
+magnitudes, this dominates the decimal formatting error. This resolves
+the previously identified serialization concern for this interface,
+subject to the explicitly supported 64-bit significand environment.
+The separate generic nonfinite-input issue in the congruence helper
+must be distinguished from its reachability with these fixed inputs.
+No original frozen source or scientific pin was modified.
+
+A diagnostic replay with finite/order checks completed the minimum, all
+109 charts and the geometry without a guard failure. Its scientific
+outputs and coefficient files were byte-identical to the untouched fresh
+run. Exact hexadecimal sidecars were compared with the exported decimals
+using rational arithmetic: 8,284 chart interval records, 436 one-sided
+chart scalars, 715 geometry interval records, three geometry summaries
+and the four consumed minimum scalars passed their directional tests.
+This addresses the fixed separator execution and its actual exports;
+it neither repairs the original helper's generic NaN contract nor
+constitutes a second interval implementation. The connection and full
+optimality audit remain pending recovery of the connection archive.
